   "start": 0.32,
   "text": "Distension, touch and vagal stimulation increase the secretion, as do gastrin, secretin, CCK, glucagon, and entero-krinin. Sympathetic stimulation inhibits it. In the first few centimeters of the duodenum, Brunner's glands add an alkaline mucus, rich in bicarbonate, that protects the wall from acid. They respond to irritation, vagal stimulation and secretin, and they are inhibited by sympathetic activity."
  }
